\pard\qc\b\fs30 MASTER SERVICES AGREEMENT\b0\fs22\par\par
\pard\sa120 Agreement No. MSA-2026-014\par
\pard\sa120 This Master Services Agreement (the Agreement) is entered into on 1 July 2026 (the Effective Date) between Meridian Industrial Solutions Pvt. Ltd., having its registered office at Industrial Estate Phase 2, Coimbatore 641021 (the Client), and Techspan Contractors LLP, having its office at 14 Lake View Road, Chennai 600028 (the Service Provider).\par
\pard\sb200\b 1. SERVICES\b0\par
\pard\sa120 1.1 The Service Provider shall provide skilled contract engineering personnel and related support services as described in each Statement of Work (SOW) executed under this Agreement.\par
\pard\sa120 1.2 Each SOW shall specify the scope, deliverables, personnel, timelines and fees. In case of conflict between this Agreement and an SOW, this Agreement prevails unless the SOW expressly states otherwise.\par
\pard\sb200\b 2. TERM\b0\par
\pard\sa120 2.1 This Agreement commences on the Effective Date and continues for an initial term of 24 months, unless terminated earlier in accordance with Clause 8.\par
\pard\sa120 2.2 The Agreement renews automatically for successive 12-month periods unless either party gives written notice of non-renewal at least 90 days before the end of the then-current term.\par
\pard\sb200\b 3. FEES AND PAYMENT\b0\par
\pard\sa120 3.1 The Client shall pay the fees set out in the applicable SOW. All fees are exclusive of GST, which shall be charged at the prevailing rate.\par
\pard\sa120 3.2 The Service Provider shall invoice monthly in arrears. The Client shall pay undisputed invoices within 45 days of receipt of a valid invoice.\par
\pard\sa120 3.3 Late payments shall attract interest at 1.0 percent per month on the overdue amount. The Client may withhold payment of any amount disputed in good faith, provided it notifies the Service Provider in writing within 15 days of receiving the invoice.\par
\pard\sb200\b 4. CONFIDENTIALITY\b0\par
\pard\sa120 4.1 Each party shall keep the other party's Confidential Information strictly confidential and shall use it solely for the purposes of this Agreement. These obligations survive termination for 5 years.\par
\pard\sb200\b 5. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY\b0\par
\pard\sa120 5.1 All work product created by the Service Provider specifically for the Client under an SOW shall be owned by the Client upon payment in full. Pre-existing materials of the Service Provider remain its property, and the Client receives a non-exclusive licence to use them as part of the deliverables.\par
\pard\sb200\b 6. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY\b0\par
\pard\sa120 6.1 The total aggregate liability of either party under this Agreement shall not exceed INR 50,00,000 (Rupees Fifty Lakh) in any contract year.\par
\pard\sa120 6.2 Neither party shall be liable for indirect, incidental or consequential losses. This limitation does not apply to breach of confidentiality, infringement of intellectual property, or fraud or wilful misconduct.\par
\pard\sb200\b 7. DATA PROTECTION AND SECURITY\b0\par
\pard\sa120 7.1 The Service Provider shall comply with the Client's information security policies when accessing Client systems and shall report any security incident affecting Client data within 24 hours of discovery.\par
\pard\sb200\b 8. TERMINATION\b0\par
\pard\sa120 8.1 Either party may terminate this Agreement for convenience by giving 90 days written notice to the other party.\par
\pard\sa120 8.2 Either party may terminate immediately by written notice if the other party commits a material breach that remains uncured 30 days after written notice, or becomes insolvent.\par
\pard\sb200\b 9. GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTES\b0\par
\pard\sa120 9.1 This Agreement is governed by the laws of India. Disputes shall first be referred to senior management of both parties for 30 days. Unresolved disputes shall be settled by arbitration under the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996, by a sole arbitrator, with the seat and venue in Chennai. The language of arbitration shall be English.\par
\pard\sb200\b 10. NOTICES\b0\par
\pard\sa120 10.1 Notices must be in writing and sent by registered post or email to the addresses above. Notices to the Client shall be marked for the attention of the Legal Department.\par
\pard\sa120 Signed for the Client: Ramesh Iyer, Managing Director\par
\pard\sa120 Signed for the Service Provider: Latha Narayanan, Designated Partner\par
